{
  "_comment": "Conformance cases for parse_plan, reading a capture plan Rail Center serves and checking it against the field reference, read as a policy bundle is: a field the reader doesn't know is passed over. `plan` is the worked example in railxia/docs' design/2026-11-10-rc-dg-capture-plan/design.md at 95b5c7b (its section 2), its body paths under request, as are a query's and a path segment's (in place of the reference's body, query and path roots); each case is that plan with `patch` applied (RFC 6902: add, remove, replace). `expect.valid` is whether parse_plan accepts it; `conditions`, where given, are the first entry's as read (`valid`, `unknown`, `invalid`), each checked when compiled. Not here, since they're the caller's to check: the content_hash's form, the schema_version's major, the agent, the redaction_version. The proxy's ceilings: window_seconds 60 to 86400, max_groups_per_window up to 100000, max_steps_per_window up to 1000000, max_unsent_windows up to 1000.",
